<title>USA: Tech IPOs long-term performers -- Morgan Stanley.</title>
<headline>Tech IPOs long-term performers -- Morgan Stanley.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Initial public offerings of technology firms have proved to be strong performers in the long term, according to a recent study.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley's Technology IPO Yearbook, which analyzes data on all of the sector's IPOs from 1980 through January 1997, said that of the 987 firms covered, 621, or 63 percent have gained in price since their IPO, or were acquired at a premium to the IPO price.</p>
<p>The remaining 37 percent were flat or down.</p>
</text>
